ாட்சி","gloss":"sight"}],"gloss":"sight","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நின்னோடு","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"},{"text":"ஓடு","lemma":"ஓடு","gloss":"sociative case marker"}],"gloss":"with you"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உடன்உறைவு","parts":[{"text":"உடன்","lemma":"உடன்","gloss":"together"},{"text":"உறைவு","lemma":"உறைவு","gloss":"living"}],"gloss":"living together"},{"surface":"ஆக்குக","parts":[{"text":"ஆக்கு","lemma":"ஆக்கு","gloss":"make"},{"text":"க","lemma":"க","gloss":"optative suffix"}],"gloss":"may it make"},{"surface":"உயர்ந்த","parts":[{"text":"உயர்","lemma":"உயர்","gloss":"rise"},{"text":"ந்","lemma":"ந்","gloss":"sandhi"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"த்","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"supreme"},{"surface":"பாலே","parts":[{"text":"பால்","lemma":"பால்","gloss":"fate/destiny"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"fate indeed"}]}],"literal":"A male monkey to eat, torn, drum-resembling big fruit / for the bow-bearing hill-dwellers, staying food becomes / O lord of the mountain-possessing land! O greatly generous Pari! / For our mingled friendship, you did not act fittingly, you, to me / you sulked and became so, during the years you protected me / Not permitting the friendship of great worthy excellence / \"Stay back, without letting us come together,\" saying / you are of such nature, therefore to you, then, I / did not approach immediately, even though I am indeed so / showing like this life, in the next life / without any gap in sight, with you / may the supreme fate make our living together!","translation":"O Pari, lord of the mountainous land where the huge jackfruit, resembling a drum and torn open by monkeys to eat, becomes the daily food of the bow-bearing hill-dwellers! You did not act fittingly toward our deep friendship. In all the years you protected me, you have now sulked and left me behind. Not allowing me to come along with you, which would befit our highly worthy and excellent friendship, you said, 'Stay back!' and departed. Since you have acted thus, even though I did not immediately join you in death, may supreme fate make us live together in the next life without any gap in our meeting, just as we did in this life!","modern":"மந்திகள் உண்ணும்படி கிழிந்த, முழவு போன்ற பெரிய பலாப்பழம், வில்லேந்திய குறவர்களுக்குத் தங்கி உண்ணும் உணவாகும் மலைநாட்டின் தலைவனே! பெருவள்ளல் பாரியே! நம்முடைய கலந்த நட்பிற்குப் பொருந்தாதவாறு நீ என்னிடம் நடந்துகொண்டாய். என்னை நீ பாதுகாத்த ஆண்டுகளில் இப்போது என்னோடு பிணங்கித் தனியே சென்றுவிட்டாய். பெருமைமிக்க நம் நட்பிற்குப் பொருந்தாமல், 'என்னுடன் சேர்ந்து வர வேண்டாம், நீ இங்கேயே தங்கிவிடு' என்று கூறிவிட்டுச் சென்றுவிட்டாய். நீ அப்படிச் செய்ததால், நான் உன்னுடன் உடனே இறக்காமல் உயிர் பிழைத்திருந்தாலும், இந்தப்பிறவியைப் போலவே மறுபிறவியிலும் இடைவெளியில்லாத சந்திப்போடு உன்னுடன் கூடி வாழும் வாழ்க்கையை உயர்ந்த விதி நமக்கு உண்டாக்கட்டும்!","explanation":"This poem is spoken by the great poet Kapilar on the death of his beloved friend and patron, King Vēḷ Pāri. Kapilar is filled with grief and a sense of betrayal because Pāri departed from this world alone, leaving him behind. He addresses Pāri, saying that leaving him behind does not fit the greatness of their deep friendship. Although Kapilar did not immediately die alongside Pāri, he is now preparing to end his life through starvation (vaṭakkiruttal). He prays that supreme destiny will unite them in the next birth without any separation, just as they lived in this life. The opening image of the jackfruit, which is so large that it feeds the hill-dwellers after being torn by monkeys, subtly evokes Pāri's boundless generosity.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.7],[1.7,2.1],[2.1,2.96],[3.3,3.81],[3.88,4.38],[4.45,4.8],[4.8,5.2],[5.2,5.6],[5.6,6.0],[6.0,6.2],[6.2,6.5],[6.5,6.9],[6.9,7.7],[7.7,8.3],[8.3,8.8],[8.8,8.95],[8.95,9.24],[9.24,9.98],[9.98,10.4],[10.4,11.0],[11.06,11.24],[11.3,11.9],[11.9,12